In article <1ptk39INNjpg@titan.ucs.umass.edu>, jason@titan.ucs.umass.edu (jason bastek) writes:
|> i would like to be able to use nethack in tty-mode again.  i can't
|> seem to find any command-line switches which force tty-mode, and
|> fooling around with my env. vars. doesn't seem to help.  can anybody
|> offer some advice, other than recompiling the whole thing?
|> 
(this is csh, but you'll figure it out)

setenv NETHACKOPTIONS "window:tty"       Use tty-mode
setenv NETHACKOPTIONS "window:X11"       Use X11 graphics
(put your other options after the window...mode option)
